<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Wrench Theory collects, uses and protects information, including cookies and Google AdSense advertising." updated="November 10, 2026">
  <p>This policy explains what information Wrench Theory ("we") collects when you visit this website, how it is used, and the choices you have.</p>
  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Newsletter.</b> If you subscribe, we store your email address to send you new articles. You can unsubscribe at any time from any email.</li>
    <li><b>Contact form.</b> If you write to us, we receive your name, email address and message, and use them only to answer you.</li>
    <li><b>Usage data.</b> Like most websites, we collect anonymous statistics such as pages visited, device type and approximate location, through analytics tools.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Cookies and advertising</h2>
  <p>This site may show ads served by Google AdSense. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website or other websites.</p>
  <p>Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visits to this site and/or other sites on the Internet. You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>, or opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">www.aboutads.info</a>.</p>
  <p>To learn how Google uses information from sites that use its services, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener" target="_blank">How Google uses data when you use our partners' sites or apps</a>. More detail is in our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>We may use Google Analytics to understand how the site is used. Google Analytics collects information such as the pages you visit and how long you stay, using cookies. You can install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</p>
  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <p>We use the information above to run and improve the site, send the newsletter you asked for, answer messages, and show advertising that keeps the content free. We do not sell your personal information.</p>
  <h2>Data retention and security</h2>
  <p>We keep newsletter and contact information only as long as needed for those purposes, and we use reputable service providers to store it securely.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live (for example under Canada's PIPEDA or the EU's GDPR), you may have the right to access, correct or delete your personal information, and to withdraw consent. To make a request, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is intended for adults and students in technical training. We do not knowingly collect information from children under 13.</p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy. The date at the top of the page shows the latest version.</p>
</LegalLayout>
